  <prompt>
    Amend EnvelopeBudget.User (currently 300 — a binding golden-utterance merge-gate) to accommodate the profile fragment; size from the actual rendered length (expected ~500-700). Render the fragment deterministically (ordinal-ordered multi-selects, canonicalized prefs JSON — no map-order nondeterminism). Re-baseline the golden-utterance gate + the eval prompt-cache prefix. Define a latency budget + caching decision for the second per-turn Dataverse read; soft-fail-to-null.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET developer expert in the ContextEnvelope renderer, EnvelopeBudget, the golden-utterance eval gate, and the IdentityNormalizationService caching precedent.
  </role>

  <goal>
    EnvelopeBudget.User raised to a value sized from the rendered fragment (code-review sign-off recorded per ADR-tension Path B). The fragment renders byte-stably (ContextEnvelopeRendererTests updated). The golden-utterance gate + eval prompt-cache prefix are re-baselined green. A latency budget + caching decision (cite or reject the IdentityNormalizationService Redis 10-min TTL) is documented, with soft-fail-to-null.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      ADR-tension #2 is Path B (project-scoped amendment): the 300 ceiling is intentionally raised, not silently squeezed. Byte-stability protects the prompt-cache prefix (NFR-02/04). The profile adds a systemuser→sprk_userprofile read on the hot bind path (NFR-03).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Context/</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/ (ContextEnvelopeRendererTests)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">EnvelopeBudget.User is a ratified constant + golden-utterance merge-gate — the change is a documented Path-B amendment with code-review sign-off (CLAUDE.md §6.5), not a silent edit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-042">Fragment renders stated profile only; canonicalize prefs JSON deterministically.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Byte-stability: ordinal-ordered multi-selects, canonical JSON, no map-order nondeterminism. Update ContextEnvelopeRendererTests + re-baseline the eval prefix.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Soft-fail-to-null on the profile read (NFR-07); document the latency budget + caching decision explicitly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Measure publish-size; ≤60 MB.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
